      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Director of Creative Content LOCATION Main Campus - Buies Creek NC Job Code 3678 # of Openings 1 Apply Now Position:                       Director of Creative Content Department:                 Athletics Status:                          Full Time Position Summary: This position is responsible for all facets of athletics video, digital and social media areas. Extensive knowledge of social media platforms and social media engagement are required. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and execute the comprehensive plan for Campbell Athletics Social Media accounts to include the social media calendars and creative content implementation Guide all of Campbell Athletics individual sport social media accounts, ensuring each account lives up to the standards and branding of the athletics department Serve as the creative content lead with oversight of other full-time department members, as well as graduate and student assistants, including interns. Point of contact for all social media technology implementation and management including Facebook, Twitter, Instagram as well as content creation in Adobe Suite. Organize, assign and execute graphic and video coverage for Campbell Athletics Work in collaboration with other external facing departments, including but not limited to marketing, communications, ticketing, sponsorships, broadcasting, revenue generation, and branding, to support Campbell’s digital outreach. Assist the Senior Associate AD for Marketing, Communications and Branding with digital brand and asset management. Recruit, organize, schedule and mentor student workers and interns for the digital media department Compile and report analytics for Campbell Athletics social and digital media Maintain and execute the budget for the digital media department Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor at all times Uphold and abide by Campbell University policies and procedures, i