      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Standardized Patients LOCATION Main Campus - Buies Creek NC Job Code 3451 # of Openings 14 Apply Now Position:                   Standardized Patient Department:             CU School of Osteopathic Medicine Status:                      Part Time Position Summary: Standardized Patients (SP) are individuals assigned to act as patients in a mock provider-patient encounter, as part of clinical skills examinations (also known as OSCEs). SPs are utilized for students enrolled in CU health programs, including DO, PA, PT, Pharmacy, etc., and are trained to portray a specific case for which a student will do a brief medical interview and/or a focused examination. SPs will provide the students with constructive feedback regarding their performance. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Maintain a professional manner in all encounters while interacting with students, faculty, fellow SPs, staff, and university personnel. Maintain confidentiality of all information regarding student performance Portray case scripts/scenarios detailing specific emotions, behaviors, and disease signs/symptoms for presentation during simulated learning situations. Present all aspects of the case as required, including the history of the current problem, with appropriate affect/behavior and physical findings. Remain in character during the entire encounter with the student. Accurately record evaluation of student performance Provide students with constructive feedback regarding their performance on the exercise either in written or verbal format. Complete Peer Review on fellow SPs for quality assurance and communicate with the SP director or staff about inconsistencies. Complete video review and self-assessments Assist in other SP-related duties such as training, quality improvement, OSCE support, educational activities, or any other job-related duties as assigned. Receive ongoing feedback and modify behaviors accordingly. Keep the SP director updated on changes in availability. Be able to work flexible hours and be on an on-call basis. Must be available for Pre/Post-OSCE briefings. Education: High School Diploma/GED Experience: Previous SP experience or acting experience preferred but not required. Other skills important to this position: Excellent interpersonal and communications skills (both oral and written) Bilingual preferred but not required. Improvisational skills when necessary Commitment to university and program values/mission Medical knowledge is preferred but not required. Physical Demands : SPs must be able to: move all extremities without difficulty, step up and down from an exam table, and change from clothing to a gown. No invasive procedures will be performed. Mental Demands : (complexity of duties, decision-making responsibilities, etc.) Ability to understand oral and written information and organize thoughts and ideas into effective forms of communication. Deliver scripted performances. Remember and record student performance evaluations. To Apply For This Position: Campbell University is unable to accept paper or email applications. Interested parties may submit their candidacy by clicking on the “Apply Now” button , or, if you are viewing this posting via an outside source, visit us online at http://www.campbell.edu/employment/ to apply. IMPORTANT: A cover letter, CV, or resume, and contact information for three professional references are requested as part of the application process. Applications without these attachments may be considered incomplete. If you have any questions, or if you are an individual with a disability and need assistance completing an application for employment contact the Human Resources Department at 910-893-1256 or email employment@campbell.edu .  Campbell University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Campbell University maintains a continuing policy of nondiscrimination in employment. It is our policy to provide equal opportunity in 